<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-08-26T21:43:21+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Wed, 26 Aug 2026 21:43:21 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Ashka Shah, the 17-year-old New York student who studied how a cancer-driving protein]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133543660.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A student from New York has pioneered a groundbreaking technique aimed at halting the growth of cancer cells. This research focuses on a crucial protein linked to the rapid development of tumors. By inhibiting the harmful activity of this protein, her method preserves the viability of healthy cells. She gained national acclaim as a finalist in a prestigious science competition, illuminating a promising new pathway for precision cancer therapies.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-ashka-shah-the-17-year-old-new-york-student-who-studied-how-a-cancer-driving-protein-enters-the-cell-nucleus-and-found-a-way-to-block-its-harmful-signalling-while-preserving-its-normal-function/articleshow/133543660.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-ashka-shah-the-17-year-old-new-york-student-who-studied-how-a-cancer-driving-protein-enters-the-cell-nucleus-and-found-a-way-to-block-its-harmful-signalling-while-preserving-its-normal-function/articleshow/133543660.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T20:54:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133545117,imgsize-606593.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US colleges are rolling out three-year bachelor's degrees in 120 programmes across 26 states]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133540572.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[US colleges are increasingly offering three-year bachelor's degree programmes that require 90 credits instead of the traditional 120. The programmes are now available or announced in 26 states, with 119 reduced-credit programmes identified by RAND. Supporters say they can save students time and money, while critics question their impact on learning, professional licensing, graduate admissions and employer acceptance.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/education/news/american-colleges-are-rolling-out-90-credit-three-year-bachelors-degrees-in-nearly-120-programmes-across-26-states-cutting-a-year-off-college-and-potentially-saving-students-up-to-20000/articleshow/133540572.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/education/news/american-colleges-are-rolling-out-90-credit-three-year-bachelors-degrees-in-nearly-120-programmes-across-26-states-cutting-a-year-off-college-and-potentially-saving-students-up-to-20000/articleshow/133540572.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T20:39:41+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133541534,imgsize-118891.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Holly Madison won’t sell her ‘haunted’ LA home; lists it for rent at $9,500 a month]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133541627.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Holly Madison has listed her historic Tudor-style Los Angeles home for $9,500 a month after deciding not to sell it. She bought the property for just under $1.5 million in 2012 and has described it as a fairytale-like home. The house was also investigated for paranormal activity in 2021. Madison says she may eventually keep the property for retirement and pass it on to her children.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/holly-madison-bought-a-los-angeles-fairytale-home-for-under-1-5-million-in-2012-she-now-refuses-to-sell-the-allegedly-haunted-house-and-is-renting-it-for-9500-a-month/articleshow/133541627.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/holly-madison-bought-a-los-angeles-fairytale-home-for-under-1-5-million-in-2012-she-now-refuses-to-sell-the-allegedly-haunted-house-and-is-renting-it-for-9500-a-month/articleshow/133541627.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T20:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133543036,imgsize-149191.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[3 teenagers killed, 4 injured in Brooklyn highway crash]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133543936.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/3-teenagers-kill