://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/singapore-will-pay-about-55000-in-support-for-each-child-why-the-country-is-paying-parents-to-have-babies/articleshow/133538724.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/singapore-will-pay-about-55000-in-support-for-each-child-why-the-country-is-paying-parents-to-have-babies/articleshow/133538724.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T16:41:48+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133538935,imgsize-1057675.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Michigan puts $6.5 million toward 22,650 Keweenaw acres as conservation fund tops $1.4 billion]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133538900.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Michigan’s Natural Resources Trust Fund is marking 50 years of supporting land conservation and outdoor recreation. Created in 1976 using earnings from state-owned oil, gas and mineral revenues, the fund has awarded nearly $1.4 billion so far. Its latest grants include $6.5 million to acquire nearly 22,650 acres in the Keweenaw Peninsula, along with funding for parks, trails, waterfront areas and recreation projects across Michigan.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1976-michigan-created-a-conservation-fund-from-oil-gas-and-mineral-revenues-50-years-later-it-has-awarded-nearly-1-4-billion-and-is-putting-6-5-million-toward-almost-22650-keweenaw-acres/articleshow/133538900.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1976-michigan-created-a-conservation-fund-from-oil-gas-and-mineral-revenues-50-years-later-it-has-awarded-nearly-1-4-billion-and-is-putting-6-5-million-toward-almost-22650-keweenaw-acres/articleshow/133538900.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T18:14:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133539635,imgsize-140737.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A New Zealand sailor spent years living alone on a remote Cook Islands atoll across 3 separate stays]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133539848.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Suwarrow atoll, once the secluded refuge of hermit Tom Neale, has transformed into the Cook Islands' inaugural conservation sanctuary. After Neale spent sixteen years in seclusion on Anchorage Island, the atoll was designated as a national park and bird haven. This vital area now protects critical seabird nesting grounds and marine ecosystems, allowing Neale's legacy to be honored through his preserved hut and a tribute on the island.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-new-zealand-sailor-spent-years-living-alone-on-a-remote-cook-islands-atoll-across-three-separate-stays-a-year-after-his-final-stay-ended-suwarrow-was-declared-a-national-park/articleshow/133539848.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-new-zealand-sailor-spent-years-living-alone-on-a-remote-cook-islands-atoll-across-three-separate-stays-a-year-after-his-final-stay-ended-suwarrow-was-declared-a-national-park/articleshow/133539848.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T17:21:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133540062,imgsize-1119008.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Prince Harry, Meghan and children arrive in UK after 6 years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.co